<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fomboni</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fomboni is the main town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moheli">Moheli</a> (Mwali), the smallest of the main islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>. It was the seat of the sultans of Moheli in the 19th century, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramanetaka">Ramanetaka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djoumbe-fatima">Djoumbe Fatima</a>, and its court life was shaped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> culture. It is now the capital of the autonomous island of Moheli within the Union of the Comoros.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fomboni.jpg" alt="Fomboni" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: alKomor.com · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fomboni-Ship.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
